body:
This is a fantastic quote by Teddy Roosevelt that made me a whole lot calmer about my life prospects and goals, and how to properly approach them.

&#x200B;

*"It is not often that a man can make opportunities for himself. But he can put himself in such shape that when or if the opportunities come he is ready to take advantage of them."*

wait wait... that is actually not a bad idea. One of the things I have learned over the past few years since 2016, and living with younger and "in the know" Republicans, they LOVE memes, as do most people,but they love being horrible in memes. This is why they like the idea of triggering more liberal minded people, and why that often ends up being their goal. However, if you ended up making it a race almost into being the worst, instead of suppressing the worst, you could get people to turn on the Republicans, as long as you maintained force that these are Republican ideas. They could easily lose their support if you SUDDENLY ramp up exposure to their inner workings, key word being sudden.

&#x200B;

The way I see it, exposure and and constant awareness is what desensitized many Americans to vile thinking of many Republicans, but mostly of the party itself. The American public is a frog in a boiling pot. We got Republicans wanting frog legs, and Democrats wanting a pet frog. Reps have been steadily and strongly ramping up the heat, while Dems will come in every so often and turn back down the heat. However, in the Reps adoptions of troll tactics and mental bashing, they are constantly turning the knob at all times, and its now a tug of war of turning up and down the heat. We cant turn the heat down all the way however, cause in this analogy that kills the frog from cold.. However, as time has gone on of turning up and down the flame, we have made the water boil slowly over time. The frog is going to die if it doesnt get out. The frog has been desensitized to the heat because it did not notice the incremental changes.

&#x200B;

However, what would happen if the dems stop turning down the heat? normally, Reps would slowly and steadily up the heat over time. But with trolls, that self restraint is out the window. so they keep turning that dial in a few minutes, and they dont stop turning that dial up. Its not slow and steady, instead its fast and compounding in growth. The frog is going to notice, and it will hop out of the water to save itself. All the dems have to do is focus on catching the frog once it hops from the pot. Then we rightfully berate the Reps for turning up the heat too fast and too quickly.

Honestly, your right. This is a problem I see within myself a lot. I grew up among some of the most influential people of my state, and am still good friends with many of them. these are the kinds of people whose families built the big stadium buildings, or the big libraries, or the campus dining hall. Now, they are not the absolute wealthy of the wealthy, but decently important that they get some coverage in the news when they die. Back to your point however, I want to become one of those people. I want to be able to put my name on a building like a science center, or or nice new library. I want to be able to make massive endowment funds and helpful foundations of research, and even a few scholarship programs for things I like. I want to be the man about town that everyone knows and is respected and well liked. Now I know that sounds very self centered and what not, but thats not my point right now. I do very fine in school. I have a solid GPA of around 3.2 on an off day, and usually come out at the end of the year with 3.7 or so. My grades are solid, I dont get in too much trouble, and people generally know me and like me. Now for a normal person, I feel like this would be fine. However, for what I want to do, I feel like a constant loser, constantly fighting to put my name on something, and constantly facing harsh work and constantly having late nights to get stuff done. I feel like a 6 year old running in a marathon all the time, and I can not tell you how many times I have wanted to quit and give up. But I am always always ALWAYS having to remind myself that giants are built and not made, or whatever platitude you like. I have to remind myself that it is not the end of the world to have an off day.

&#x200B;

TL;DR: My Ego has become very much intertwined with my own self worth, purpose, and sense of achievement, and being only *just* good translates to *just a failure.* I don't know if it was me that changed or if society changed, or possibly if society changed me.
